# Device code indexes with 32-bit ints on purpose: a 64-bit multiply costs extra instructions in the hot loops of
# every kernel. The widening check would demand a cast at each of these sites; overflow is instead reviewed where a
# buffer can exceed 2^31 elements (expert pool, PLE table), and those offsets are computed in 64 bit explicitly.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result
